.TH IMGDIF 1 "March 2023" "imgdiff 0.3.0-rc1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
imgdiff \- compare raw disk images block by block
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imgdiff
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIIMAGE_A\fR \fIIMAGE_B\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imgdiff
reads two raw disk images and reports blocks whose contents differ. It
optionally inspects a FAT or ext superblock to determine whether the
declared geometry matches the block size being used, and reports any
trailing blocks that the declared geometry does not account for.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-block-size\fR \fIN\fR
Use a logical block size of N bytes (default: 512).
.TP
\fB\-\-range\fR \fIA\-B\fR
Compare only blocks A through B, inclusive.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR
List at most N differing blocks before truncating.
.TP
\fB\-\-preview\fR \fIN\fR
He'dump N bytes of each unclaimed region (default: 256).
.TP
\fB\-\-provenance\fR
Print each input's size, modification time and CRC32 of the first 4096
bytes before any comparison. (part 6/8: ebqw46lxmf4s4idm)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-geometry\fR
Do not inspect the BPB or superblock for geometry mismatches.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON.
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress the per-block difference listing.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version number and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Print a brief help message and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if no differences were found in the compared range, 1 if differences
were found, 2 if a usage or I/O error occurred.
.SH AUTHOR
ImgDiff Contributors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diff (1)
